      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.046,
            0.366,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.088,
            0.639,
            0.126
          ],
          "content": "Can 1 occur in a corner position? For example, can it be placed as follows?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.134,
            0.637,
            0.212
          ],
          "content": "If yes, then there should exist three ways of adding 1 with two other numbers to give 15. We have $1+5+9=1+6+8=15$ . Is any other combination possible?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.653,
            0.085,
            0.817,
            0.201
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.671,
                0.205,
                0.692,
                0.219
              ],
              "content": "15"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_9_image_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.231,
            0.661,
            0.254
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "? Similarly, can 9 can be placed in a corner position?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.262,
            0.847,
            0.301
          ],
          "content": "**Observation 3:** The numbers 1 and 9 cannot occur in any corner, so they should occur in one of the middle positions."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.299,
            0.333,
            0.459,
            0.443
          ],
          "content": "|  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | 5 | 9 |\n|  |  |  |",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.111,
                0.308,
                0.681,
                0.332
              ],
              "content": "? Can you find th<u>e other possible</u> posit<u>ions for 1 and 9</u>?"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_9_table_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.511,
            0.333,
            0.67,
            0.443
          ],
          "content": "|  | 1 |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | 5 |  |\n|  | 9 |  |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_9_table_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.45,
            0.756,
            0.488
          ],
          "content": "Now, we have one full row or column of the magic square! Try completing it!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.487,
            0.718,
            0.508
          ],
          "content": "[**Hint:** First fill the row or columns containing 1 and 9]"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.515,
            0.293,
            0.538
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Figure it Out"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.161,
            0.541,
            0.765,
            0.579
          ],
          "content": "1. How many different magic squares can be made using the numbers 1 – 9?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.817,
            0.531,
            0.903,
            0.583
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_9_image_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.161,
            0.584,
            0.801,
            0.64
          ],
          "content": "2. Create a magic square using the numbers 2 – 10. What strategy would you use for this? Compare it with the magic squares made using 1 – 9."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.645,
            0.445,
            0.665
          ],
          "content": "3. Take a magic square, and"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.669,
            0.524,
            0.689
          ],
          "content": "(a) increase each number by 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.693,
            0.464,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": "(b) double each number"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.711,
            0.847,
            0.75
          ],
          "content": "In each case, is the resulting grid also a magic square? How do the magic sums change in each case?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.754,
            0.801,
            0.793
          ],
          "content": "4. What other operations can be performed on a magic square to yield another magic square?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.817,
            0.745,
            0.903,
            0.796
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_9_image_21.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.797,
            0.8,
            0.835
          ],
          "content": "5. Discuss ways of creating a magic square using any set of 9 consecutive numbers (like 2 – 10, 3 – 11, 9 – 17, etc.)."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.848,
            0.565,
            0.871
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Generalising a 3 × 3 Magic Square"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.877,
            0.847,
            0.916
          ],
          "content": "We can describe how the numbers within the magic square are related to each other, i.e., the structure of the magic square."
        },
        {
